{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1532769-optional-magicks-book","id":1532769,"title":"Optional Magicks Book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-17T10:47:25-07:00","id":1532769,"title":"Optional Magicks Book","content":"What it says on the tin. What would you want in a Mage book on optional magic systems?<br /> <br /> It seems to me it should be a buffet of options form mere chrome to reshaping the whole system with analysis of how gameplay would be changed. <br /> <br /> I'd especially want a thick chapter on retooling Mage Magic to genres like adventure, mystery, gothic romance, Space Opera, four color supers, and more.<br /> <br /> But what's your take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T18:57:11-07:00","id":1532789,"title":"","content":"That book already exists \u2014 only, it was written for <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>. I'm referring to the <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/82216/Mage-Chroniclers-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Chronicler's Guide</a>, a book which deconstructed <b>Awakening</b> and then speculated on how the pieces could be reassembled to do other things. <br /> <br /> <i>Genres</i>? You have Action Horror, Pulp, Epic Fantasy, Faustian Sorcery, Lucid Sleepers (i.e., what if Magic was public knowledge?), Punk, and Noir. <i>Variant Magic?</i> You get Gifted Science, the Psychic Sphere, and Minor Variants: All For One and One For All (where all magic must be cast by groups), Pop More Pills, Pillheads (where magic is linked to drug use), Supernal Objects (where magic comes from magic items), and Ritual Magic (where all magic requires lengthy rituals). <i>Variants on what mages are like</i>? You get deconstructions of <b>Awakening</b>'s Paths and Orders, followed by possible alternatives to each. <br /> <br /> And then you get a series of Chronicle ideas: <i>the Andrews Family Coven</i> (what if families of mages existed?), <i>The Bones of the World</i> (a chronicle about literary geeks seeking out mysterious and mystical tomes), <i>the Chosen Path</i> (what if the Awakening was something you could seek out?), <i>Diamond</i> (where the Orders are more like nations than secret societies), <i>the Epistolary Chronicle</i> (where the roleplaying is done by writing letters in-character), <i>Furyland</i> (mages at war), <i>Into the Shadow</i> (where the spirit world is the focus of the game), <i>Jianghu Modern</i> (things like \u201cCrouching Tiger Hidden Dragon\u201d, but with magic instead of martial arts), <i>the Legacy Chronicle</i> (where Legacies replace Paths and Orders as the central organizing principle of the game), <i>Mad with Power</i> (mage in the style of Lovecraft), <i>Over the Falls</i> (where the protagonists break the rules; in this case, by not bringing to Paths when everyone else does), <i>Protecting the Sleepers</i> (well-meaning heroes who must resist the temptation to abuse their powers), <i>the Secret of Shangri-La</i> (what if Magic was inherently evil, but mages aren't?), <i>Taking Over</i> (where political intrigue is front and center), and <i>White Wolf Comics Presents: the Cabal</i> (superheroes). <br /> <br /> No science fiction, unfortunately; though the \u201cblue book\u201d supplements <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/87936/Mirrors-Bleeding-Edge\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Bleeding Edge</a> and <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/87937/Mirrors-Infinite-Macabre\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Infinite Macabre</a> do this in a more general way for cyberpunk and space opera, respectively.<br /> <hr />This sets the standard that Astromancer's proposed supplement should strive for. Obviously, <b>Awakening</b> isn't <b>Ascension</b>; but an awful lot of it translates; and what doesn't translate directly can still speak ideas. For instance, Gifted Science: in the above book, this is a set of system hacks that take a magic system that's designed with mysticism in mind and retools it to represent esoteric science. Not <i>just</i> relabeling things, but also some consideration of actual rules differences. I wouldn't mind \u201cOther Magicks\u201d including something in it to the effect of \u201cwhat if the Enlightened Science pioneered by the Technocracy <i>really is</i> (subtly) distinct from Awakened Magick? More generally, what if Magick <i>in general</i> was a bit less unified than <b>M20</b> posits, and mages practicing different styles of Magick actually use slight variants of the default Magick system instead of the game being in danger of declaring that magical style is just window dressing? That could, in fact, be the core theme of the book: what if it <i>isn't</i> \u201call the same thing\u201d after all? Maybe call it <b>Fractured Magick</b>\u2026 Or maybe it <i>is</i> all the same thing, but it's all a <i>different</i> \u201csame thing\u201d. <br /> <br /> The \u201cMagick is hereditary\u201d and \u201cMagick can be chosen\u201d are also options I'd like to see explored in the context of <b>M20</b>. I'm also currently looking into revising my \u201cAcolyte Magic\u201d hack to feature what would amount to a combination of <i>The Chosen Path</i> and <i>Faustian Sorcery</i>: Awakening to Magick <i>can</i> be pursued; but the means of doing so has some sort of price attached to it. I'd be curious what the <i>Over the Falls</i> counterpart might look like, if it's even possible: in contrast to <b>Awakening</b> and its \u201cfive Paths\u201d system, <b>Ascension</b> is <i>very</i> open on what it allows. So a mage who \u201cbreaks the rules\u201d would be weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T00:55:58-07:00","id":1533740,"title":"","content":"Get a hold on Gurps Thaumatology and Gurps Fantasy. Both books can change completely the way you play Ascension. Thaumatology gives you the tools to design the perfect magic mechanics, and Gurps Fantasy gives you a gold mine of ideas for creating unique settings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":